## Nuke build outputs (dotnet test results / ReportGenerator output; the original
## workflow wrote these under CI-only paths and never gitignored them - now that
## `nuke Test`/`nuke Coverage` are easy to run locally too, ignore them for real)
TestResults/
coverage/
## Nuke scratch dir (build.schema.json and parameters.json ARE tracked)
.nuke/temp/

## Knowledge-graph output (/graphify). Whitelist: ignore everything, then re-include
## only the parts that are portable AND not cheaply reproducible.
##
## TRACKED
##   cache/semantic/        the only part that costs tokens; content-hash keyed under a
##                          prompt-hash dir, so entries invalidate correctly. Repo-relative.
##   manifest.json          relativized per-file hashes; drives incremental --update
##   GRAPH_REPORT.md        small, human-readable
##   .graphify_labels.json  hand-written community labels — NOT reproducible by re-running
##   README.md              records this policy
##
## IGNORED
##   graph.json, graph.html derived; rewritten wholesale every build (~2.2 MB of churn)
##   cache/ast/             deterministic and free (~10s, no LLM); also embeds absolute paths
##   cache/stat-index.json  keyed by absolute path, and stores mtimes a clone resets anyway
##   .graphify_python       absolute interpreter path. Tracking it BREAKS graphify on another
##                          machine: the guard re-resolves only when the file is missing,
##                          never when it is stale. Run /graphify once on a fresh checkout.
##   .graphify_root         absolute scan root; re-derived on first use
graphify-out/*
!graphify-out/cache/
graphify-out/cache/*
!graphify-out/cache/semantic/
!graphify-out/manifest.json
!graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md
!graphify-out/.graphify_labels.json
!graphify-out/README.md

